#====================================================================
# Draft: C++17-removed constructs (std::auto_ptr, dynamic exception
#        specifications) compiled out via __cplusplus-derived feature macros
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-CXX17-REMOVED-CONSTRUCTS-COMPILE-OUT-VIA-FEATURE-MACRO
trigger_tool:           clang++|libc++|C++17|std::auto_ptr|dynamic exception specification
phase:                  compile
error_signature:        no template named 'auto_ptr' in namespace 'std'|ISO C++17 does not allow dynamic exception specifications

severity:               2
category:               cxx17-migration
match_keywords:         auto_ptr, dynamic exception specification, throw(), __cplusplus, feature macro, ODB_NO_AUTO_PTR, C++17, libc++, removed constructs, -std=c++14, migration, deprecated

title:                  C++17-removed constructs (std::auto_ptr, dynamic exception specifications) should be compiled out behind feature macros derived from __cplusplus, not by lowering -std

root_cause:             Code written against C++03/TR1 uses std::auto_ptr and dynamic exception specifications (throw(X)); both were removed by C++17. The OHOS toolchain's libc++ headers support C++17 and later only (see E130), so the platform-required -std=c++17 surfaces "no template named 'auto_ptr' in namespace 'std'" and "ISO C++17 does not allow dynamic exception specifications" (libodb 2.4.0: about 14 auto_ptr + 6 exception-spec = 20 errors across the core headers). Lowering -std is not available on this platform, so the removed constructs must be compiled out conditionally, deriving the condition from the language standard itself.

affected_scope:         Any pre-C++11 codebase built on the OHOS clang/libc++ toolchain (or any C++17-only environment): std::auto_ptr in interfaces and factories, throw() specifications on functions and operator news. The same signature must recur in every 2010s-and-earlier library of this style. Verified instance: libodb 2.4.0 core headers.

verification_cmd:       d=$(mktemp -d) && printf '#include <memory>\nstruct X{};\nint f() throw(X){return 0;}\nstd::auto_ptr<int> g(){return std::auto_ptr<int>();}\nint main(){return f()==0;}\n' > "$d/tu.cxx" && { clang++ -std=c++17 -fsyntax-only "$d/tu.cxx" ; echo "expect FAIL: no template named 'auto_ptr' + dynamic exception specification" ; clang++ -std=c++14 -fsyntax-only "$d/tu.cxx" && echo "control c++14: clean" ; }

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           feature-macro-compile-out-derived-from-cplusplus
rec_description:        Derive a feature macro from the language standard and compile the removed constructs out - zero platform macros (R8): in a central config header `#if __cplusplus >= 201703L` / `#define ODB_NO_AUTO_PTR` / `#endif`, guard the auto_ptr specializations with `#ifndef ODB_NO_AUTO_PTR`, and drop or `#if __cplusplus < 201703L`-guard the throw(X) specifications. Behavior under older standards is unchanged, the fix is upstreamable, and the same technique generalizes to any C++17-removed construct. libodb 2.4.0 needed 20 errors removed this way and then compiled clean under C++17.
rec_command:            apply the feature-macro patch and rebuild: conan create archives/l/libodb-pgsql/2.4.0 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/l/libodb-pgsql/2.4.0/patches/0001-odb-cxx17-header-compat.patch (ODB_NO_AUTO_PTR derivation in odb/details/config.hxx + guarded auto_ptr sections + removed dynamic exception specifications)

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      compat-shim-alias-header
fallback_description:   A compatibility shim/alias header providing a local auto_ptr replacement can unblock builds where the library headers cannot be patched. Honest trade-off: it masks the compatibility gap instead of fixing it, and its semantics diverge from the real (removed) std::auto_ptr - last resort only.
fallback_command:       generate a local auto_ptr shim header and inject it via CXXFLAGS as an experiment
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       lower -std globally to c++14|force -std=c++14 in the recipe|edit the SDK libc++ headers to restore auto_ptr
forbid_1_reason:        The SDK libc++ headers themselves require C++17 (the E130 direction), so lowering -std trades these errors for a wall of different failures elsewhere; editing SDK headers poisons every build on the machine.
forbid_1_consequence:   the failure migrates instead of resolving; non-shippable toolchain mutations.

similar_to:             "E130(same environment, opposite direction: E130 raises -std to fix header incompatibility, this entry cleans up constructs removed after the raise), E198(C++ standard evolution deprecation family), E293(same error family - dynamic exception specifications under C++17 - but coverage differs: E293 handles only throw(X)+register from 2003-era code and its rec is a warning downgrade via -Wno-error=dynamic-exception-spec/-Wno-error=register toolchain flags, with a noexcept(false)-rewrite fallback, no feature-macro solution and no std::auto_ptr coverage; this entry adds the auto_ptr specializations compiled out behind __cplusplus-derived feature macros: same family, different solution, complementary not duplicate)"

principles:             P-PATCH-001, platform-agnostic-fix, real-evidence-over-assumption

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-cxx17-removed-constructs-compile-out-via-feature-macro.md
